          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the final trick of the hand. The winner of the final trick is paid by the other players according to chips won; winning all 16 tricks wins all chips. Session may end with Gobah (five more deals), the last being Tashi Gobah.',
          gameplay: '1. **Setup**: Tiles are stacked (wood wall). Each player draws 16 tiles. 2. **Tile Hierarchy**: Civil (Wen) has 11 ranksâ€”6-6 (Heaven) highest; Military (Wu) has 10 ranksâ€”2-4 and 1-2 (The Supreme) highest. 3. **Lead**: Winner of previous trick (or dealer on first) leads 1â€“4 tiles (single, pair, or set of 3â€“4 matching). 4. **Follow**: Others must play the same number of tiles. To win the trick, beat every tile in the lead with higher-ranking tiles of the same suit. 5. **Bury**: If you cannot beat the lead, bury tiles face down (waste). 6. **Final Trick**: Winning the 16th trick scores 1 point (2 if won with a Supreme set). First team to target (11 or 21) wins.',
          keyRules: [
            'No Trump suit: The Civil/Military distinction acts as a dual-suit system.',
            'Waste Tiles: Tiles buried face down cannot be retrieved or inspected.',
            'Dealer rotation only happens if the non-dealing team wins the final trick.',
            'Players can lead singles, pairs, or sets of 3â€“4 tiles of matching rank or suit.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Save your big tiles (6-6, 1-1, 4-4) for the end. It doesn't matter if you lose the first 15 tricks as long as you have the highest tile for the 16th.",
          intermediate: "Exhaust the opponent's 'Civil' suit early. If you have many Military tiles, lead them to force out your opponents' big Civil tiles so they can't use them to win the final trick.",
          advanced: "Set Detection: If an opponent leads a 'Double Pair', they are signaling they have a deep hand. You must decide whether to challenge them now or save your tiles to 'bury' theirs later.",
          tips: [
            "In Bagchen, 'The Supreme' (2-4 / 1-2) is the ultimate trap. Use it to win a trick that allows you to lead a set your opponent can't beat.",
            "Communicate with your partner through your discards. If you bury a high Civil tile, it tells your partner you are 'running dry' on that suit.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
